3. Related work
3.1. Goal-conditioned imitation learning
GCIL is a subdomain of IL that focuses on training agents, particularly robots, to achieve specific goals by conditioning the learning process on goal information. GCIL methods can generally be categorized into two main classes: non-diffusion-based methods and diffusion-based
